	"Name": "Time goes by like a multiplayer",
	"Author": "inju768",
	"Description": "Don't you like it when you're talking to one NPC and all the NPCs pause as if they're under a spell? Does time stop every time you go fishing and your fishing day feels too long? Do you want to make your day off by playing Junimo Kart or playing games, but are you frustrated that the time doesn't pass? We have prepared a mode for those people. We added a few lines of script that makes single-player mode recognize multiplayer mode, so time now passes in single-player mode like multiplayer mode. You no longer have to do stupid things with two computers.\n<br />\n<br />It's compatible with most modes. This is because it's just a few lines of script that make single play be recognized as multi-play. However, modes that are stated to be unavailable for multiplay are most likely not compatible with this mode.\u00A0And since this mode only allows 'recognition' of single play as multiplay, it's likely that multiplay only modes are also incompatible\n<br />\n<br />There are two versions: a version in which time stops during events (festivals, event cutscenes, etc.), and a version in which time flows in all situations.",
